## 2026-08-10 - Cooldown-Aware Scheduling and Repository Cleanup

- **Summary**: Implemented, secured, merged, and live-validated dynamic top.gg cooldown retries; corrected GitHub Actions cleanup to keep latest 10 completed runs repository-wide.

- **Details (The 'What')**:
  - Added bounded parsing for top.gg cooldown text such as `You can vote again in about 1 hour.`
  - Supported seconds, minutes, hours, and days; singular/plural and numeric/word values.
  - Added 5-minute safety buffer and 60-second to 24-hour validation bounds.
  - Selected earliest retry timestamp across every account/bot result.
  - Stored only `{"next_vote_at": <UTC epoch>}` in a private one-day artifact.
  - Added `cooldown-retry.yml`, a credential-free five-minute dispatcher using only `actions: write`.
  - Kept fixed 07:00/19:00 WIB schedules as fallback.
  - Added branch-scoped concurrency, duplicate prevention, timestamp validation, one-shot dispatch, and self-disable lifecycle.
  - Increased test suite from 42 to 51 tests.
  - Updated README and SECURITY documentation with timing, fallback, privacy, and permission boundaries.
  - Created `tasks/lessons.md` and captured completion-verification, cross-job state, lifecycle, and cleanup-scope lessons.
  - Found live GitHub suppression of numeric timestamp job output; moved cross-job control state to same-run artifact retrieval.
  - Made workflow disable idempotent and changed disabled-workflow lookup from display name to stable filename.
  - Found cleanup scope mismatch: it retained 10 `Top.gg Auto Vote` runs but ignored other workflow histories.
  - Changed cleanup to paginate all repository Actions runs, skip active runs, keep newest 10 completed runs globally, and surface deletion failures.
  - Live cleanup reduced repository history from 59 runs to exactly 10 completed runs.
  - Merged protected PRs #11, #12, #13, and #14 with required `test` and `dependency-audit` checks.
  - Persisted global completion-verification rule in `C:\Users\alams\.gemini\config\GEMINI.md`.
  - Extended global `test_runner` skill with CI/CD control-plane E2E verification procedure.

- **Decisions (The 'Why')**:
  - Used native GitHub artifact plus temporary dispatcher because GitHub schedules are static and user rejected PATs, external schedulers, DB state, issues, and commit-based cron mutation.
  - Used approximate target plus 5–10 minutes because top.gg says `about` and GitHub scheduled events have five-minute granularity plus queue delay.
  - Kept credentials only in read-only vote job; scheduler and cleanup receive no Discord, top.gg, or Telegram credentials.
  - Treated CAPTCHA as terminal on same runner/IP; repeated retry would reuse challenge conditions.
  - Changed retention to repository-wide because README promise and user expectation referred to all GitHub Actions history, not one workflow.
  - Required live E2E checks because lint, unit tests, and required CI could not reveal GitHub control-plane semantics.

- **Verification**:
  - `python -m unittest -v`: 51 passed.
  - Python compile: passed.
  - `pip check`: no broken requirements.
  - OSV audit: no known vulnerabilities in 10 locked packages.
  - `actionlint` and YAML lint: passed.
  - Live cooldown artifact contained timestamp only.
  - Pre-due dispatcher created no vote run.
  - Due dispatcher created exactly one vote run and disabled itself.
  - Final master smoke authenticated and voted successfully.
  - Repository cleanup live count: 10 completed, 0 active.
  - Final `master`: `c3019c4`, synchronized and clean.
  - Open PRs: 0.
  - Open vulnerability alerts: 0.

- **Blockers & Open Questions**:
  - nodriver browser startup remains externally flaky on some GitHub-hosted runners; same commit also completed successful browser/vote runs.
  - Dynamic retry is created when an initial page already reports cooldown. Successful vote path does not currently extract a future cooldown timestamp.
  - Dispatcher becomes active again whenever latest vote run emits another valid cooldown artifact; current final runtime state may therefore be active after a fresh cooldown result.

- **Next Steps**:
  - Monitor next scheduled 07:00/19:00 WIB run and next natural cooldown dispatch.
  - If browser startup failures repeat, capture runner/Chrome/nodriver diagnostics and debug root cause scientifically.
  - Reassess post-success cooldown extraction only if fixed fallback schedules prove insufficient.

